							"source": " 1/4 \\bar{\\epsilon} \\Gamma^{m n p q} \\chi_{m n} \\bar{\\psi_{p}} \\Gamma_{q}^{r} \\psi_{r} e -  1/8 \\bar{\\epsilon} \\Gamma^{m n p q} \\chi_{m}^{r} \\bar{\\psi_{n}} \\Gamma_{p r} \\psi_{q} e +  1/8 \\bar{\\epsilon} \\Gamma^{m n p q} \\chi^{r}_{m} \\bar{\\psi_{n}} \\Gamma_{p r} \\psi_{q} e"
						}
					],
					"source": "\\begin{dmath*}{}\\frac{1}{4}\\,\\bar{\\epsilon} \\Gamma^{m n p q} \\chi_{m n} \\bar{\\psi_{p}} \\Gamma_{q}\\,^{r} \\psi_{r} e\\discretionary{}{}{} - \\frac{1}{8}\\,\\bar{\\epsilon} \\Gamma^{m n p q} \\chi_{m}\\,^{r} \\bar{\\psi_{n}} \\Gamma_{p r} \\psi_{q} e\\discretionary{}{}{}+\\frac{1}{8}\\,\\bar{\\epsilon} \\Gamma^{m n p q} \\chi^{r}\\,_{m} \\bar{\\psi_{n}} \\Gamma_{p r} \\psi_{q} e\\end{dmath*}"
				}
			],
			"source": "converge(tot):\n    join_gamma(tot)\n    distribute(tot)\n    eliminate_kronecker(tot)\n;\nconverge(tot):\n    sort_product(tot)\n    canonicalise(tot)\n    rename_dummies(tot)\n    collect_terms(tot)\n;"
		},
		{
			"cell_id": 5010698093421842359,
			"cell_origin": "client",
			"cell_type": "latex",
			"cells": [
				{
					"cell_id": 5010698093421842359,
					"cell_origin": "client",
					"cell_type": "latex_view",
					"source": "\\subsection*{The final cancellation}\n\nThe remaining terms all contain $\\Gamma^{mnpq}$ and five different flat indices.\nIn four dimensions they vanish because antisymmetrising over five indices gives zero\n(a Schouten identity). We make this explicit the way vN does, with the epsilon tensor and\n$\\gamma_5 = \\Gamma_1\\Gamma_2\\Gamma_3\\Gamma_4$. With our Euclidean metric,\n\\begin{equation*}\n\\Gamma^{mnpq} = \\varepsilon^{mnpq}\\gamma_5\\,,\\qquad\n\\Gamma_{mn} = -\\tfrac12\\varepsilon_{mnpq}\\Gamma^{pq}\\gamma_5\\,.\n\\end{equation*}\nWe first lower all indices on the $\\Gamma_{mn}$, so that every epsilon has all its lower\nindices together. Then the products of two epsilon tensors become Kronecker deltas, and\neverything cancels."
				}
			],
			"hidden": true,
			"source": "\\subsection*{The final cancellation}\n\nThe remaining terms all contain $\\Gamma^{mnpq}$ and five different flat indices.\nIn four dimensions they vanish because antisymmetrising over five indices gives zero\n(a Schouten identity). We make this explicit the way vN does, with the epsilon tensor and\n$\\gamma_5 = \\Gamma_1\\Gamma_2\\Gamma_3\\Gamma_4$. With our Euclidean metric,\n\\begin{equation*}\n\\Gamma^{mnpq} = \\varepsilon^{mnpq}\\gamma_5\\,,\\qquad\n\\Gamma_{mn} = -\\tfrac12\\varepsilon_{mnpq}\\Gamma^{pq}\\gamma_5\\,.\n\\end{equation*}\nWe first lower all indices on the $\\Gamma_{mn}$, so that every epsilon has all its lower\nindices together. Then the products of two epsilon tensors become Kronecker deltas, and\neverything cancels."
		},
